#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""bin/wb-sources-repair -- sources: repair tool (proposal S8).

Three modes:
  --check         Recompute P/N/A resolution for every frontmatter sources:
                  entry against the tree. Exits non-zero if any P/N/A-class
                  entry stops resolving (regression gate for CI / the 6h cron).
  --apply-a       Apply the S5 deterministic remaps (D2) page-by-page:
                  R-EXT (3), R-EVT (2), per-entry TABLE (12). Dry-run diff
                  printed by default; --yes writes the files.
  --apply-queue   D3 review-queue consumer. NOT IMPLEMENTED: D3 is on hold
                  for human review per the 2026-09-24 decisions.

HARD BOUNDARY (2026-09-24 decisions, proposal S11): this tool never touches
B/C/D-dead/E entries. No guessing ambiguous targets, no deleting citations,
no applying unresolved markers, no "fixing" E-class entries. D1+D2 only.

Usage:
  python3 bin/wb-sources-repair --check [--repo-root .]
  python3 bin/wb-sources-repair --apply-a [--repo-root .] [--yes]
"""
